Hm, I think I use this in the corpus book but  I am not sure I also do
that in the stats book. But if you look at a table, with str like so:

str(table(rep(1:4, 2)))

you see that there is an attribute dimnames, which suggests you can
need to get the names of the frequencies. This may well be one of
these that I just saw somewhere, though, I doubt I really learned that
from somewhere in a principled way.

Cheers,

